# Demo = invent until live-ready

This project’s **MetaQuotes demo** (`allow_live: false`) is the lab. Until the user
explicitly says the bot is ready for **real money**, invent aggressively:

- New signals, exits, sizing, filters, sessions, symbols, even **new algos**.
- Do not stay conservative “because the books / firehose YAML said so.”
- Books and INDEX are **fuel**, not a veto. When authors disagree, ship a flag
  and try the wilder side on demo.
- Measure it: tests, OOS / walk-forward, expectancy **after costs**. Never
  invent backtest numbers. Never promise profit.

## Hard gates (demo crazy ≠ live)

- Never set `allow_live: true` or point the runner at a real-money account.
- Never `mt5.shutdown()`.
- **Open/close on demo is allowed.** The user authorized 0.01-lot probes
  (including closing tickets) whenever a test needs it. Do not wipe the
  whole book unless the test is “flat and restart this idea.” See
  `demo-live-probes.mdc`. On every 20-minute check, actually look at
  tickets and probe if that answers a hypothesis.
- Do not start a second `run_broker_paper.py`. Do not cut `max_positions`
  unless a measured experiment needs it and the user is told.
- Unattended optimizer stays YAML-only (`allow_code_edit: false`) unless the
  user opens code edits. **This chat** may ship code inventions to demo.

When the user says go live, switch to conservative live rules. Until then:
**try it on demo.**
